    "body": "## Execution update — 2026-10-09 06:08 UTC\n\nThe first [surface-window controls run](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/actions/runs/37890734575) completed successfully on the exact head `275e8799d4947d297329073eaa3ca675d3fd0777` (attempt 1). Author and independent root audits consumed the complete original 114,785-byte ZIP: all 21 members, source/observer before-and-after receipts, six command records, and full stdout/stderr.\n\nThe original v15 proof, workspace formatting, scoped Clippy and all **10 exact Rust methods (6 new + 3 existing dependency controls + 1 existing stale-build control)** passed. The targeted methods had zero failed, ignored or measured cases. All 1,089 product input hashes match the approved registry before and after execution.\n\nThe 54 bounded surface fixtures record 18 → 9 SQL statements each; the 36 existing dependency fixtures record 8 → 4. These fixture counters establish removal of duplicate queries, with no claim about 100k or whole-build wall-clock improvement. This PR's full original CI is still being reviewed separately.\n\n## Problem\n\nA prepare pass already materializes a bounded public-surface candidate window, then can issue the same pending-work SQL again at its tail. Reuse that actual window when the final seed list exactly matches the queried list and admission stays within the original budget.\n\n## Change and resulting behavior\n\n- Keep the window local to one prepare call. Preserve the original SQL fallback when seeds expand, the window is missing, or admission bounds do not match.\n- Preserve the existing unconditional prepared-build epoch check, transactional fences, candidate ordering, budgets, and cursor behavior.\n- Add six focused Rust controls covering SQL equivalence, exact-basis requirements, replacement/removal/reopen, promotion behavior, expanded-seed fallback, and external-write epoch rejection.\n- Add one fixed-head controls workflow that also runs the three existing dependency-window controls and the existing stale-prepared-build test.\n- Follow #170: retain its reviewed snapshot batching product and current validation integration. The additional production change is confined to reconcile.rs. #170 remains available with its own actual CI evidence.\n\n## Review and execution\n\nThe actual P → R → G objects were independently reviewed before first publication:\n\n- Product: `a402e88d460179afb12e3e2dc066d62cf168c690`\n- Review: `f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175`\n- Fixed head: `275e8799d4947d297329073eaa3ca675d3fd0777`\n- Source inventory: 1,089 product inputs, 41 historical deltas, 139 validation inputs.\n- [Independent source review](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/blob/f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175/artifacts/checkpoints/p8-surface-window-controls-20261009/independent-source-review.json)\n- [Execution plan](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/blob/f66daf6088f6f6a8d990d736ee0c1213032ca175/artifacts/checkpoints/p8-surface-window-controls-20261009/original-execution-plan.json)\n\nNative Rust 1.95 rustfmt preparation completed before publication. At first publication, this head's controls run and unchanged original CI were pending. The execution update above records subsequently accepted evidence; earlier PR results are not substituted for this head. The v15 verifier changes contain only the four reviewed identity constants. Original CI, six frozen historical proof files, task definitions, and acceptance criteria are unchanged.\n\n## Current acceptance boundary\n\nNo measured speedup or additional TODO completion is claimed. This removes one eligible final query; prefix rescans across separate prepare calls remain. The original a23 formal N150 study continues unchanged and this engineering follow-up adds no prerequisite to its ten-task closure.\n\nCurrent original ledger: **192 total / 163 done / 29 remaining; 0 newly closed in this round**.\n",
